{
  "id": "COMPOUND:24208 - PROTEIN:4911",
  "verbalization": "Pinostrobin is implicated in the regulation of CD276 antigen through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Pinostrobin acts as a target for Caspase-5, which in turn is targeted by Flavipin or (Salicylato-O1,O2)silver. These compounds are all linked to the CD276 antigen, indicating a potential pathway where Pinostrobin may influence the expression or activity of CD276 through Caspase-5. The presence of multiple pathways converging on CD276 suggests that Pinostrobin may exert its effect via Caspase-5, possibly modulating the immune response or cellular signaling pathways that involve CD276. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, with Pinostrobin potentially playing a role in the regulation of CD276 through a Caspase-5-dependent mechanism.",
